Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?SystemUI:=20Bud=C3=ADk=20control=20centre=20on?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20a=20dimmed=20screen=20instead=20of=20a=20sheet?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The control centre still came down as an opaque full screen sheet (a
"garage door") with a grab handle. Like the iOS and Pixel control
centres it now floats on the current screen, which dims with the
finger (one full screen fill, 94 % of the background colour at the
end); the modules fade in and settle from slightly above and smaller
row by row as the finger moves, each in its own layer with the alpha
applied per draw, so no frame re-measures, re-records or uses an
offscreen layer. The transition no longer moves the panel and uses a
fixed swipe distance. No grab handle in the control centre and its
editor; it closes by swiping up or tapping empty space.

The notification shade keeps its sheet (OverlayShade dimBehind = false).
